Z||000010||Urchin||07-04-2001||11:27 AM||||I just can't believe it has come to this.  The possibilty of us losing the forum over spats and quarrels.  I don't know the situation between cliff and edsb52, nor is it any of my business.  But if the forum was shut down because of financial reasons or loss of interest then I guess I could deal with that.  But a few people ruining it for the rest of us and resulting in the ultimate closure of the forum is a lot harder to swallow.  I make a point of staying out of these sorts of things for a number of reasons.  My statements here I'm sure will go unnoticed,  but I just hope that in the future we can stick to topic at hand (fieros).  I agree with theogre's statements and many others that have responded to this incident.  I just learned of these events now.  No one likes to see these things drag on, and I am not trying to make that happen.  I just thought that for once I would add my two cents.   I'm glad to see that the forum has survived yet another setback, but lets all do our best to try and prevent these things before they occur.  I, as everyone else here does, appreciates this place being here, so lets all act like it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||07-04-2001||05:45 PM||||Well said Ogre!<P>Unfortunately, just telling people to behave won't work with all of them.  Thats why we have laws and rules... because cheaters will always be cheaters (or in this case, people who have the maturity level to continually conduct themselves in such an immature and nasty way online will continue to do so).  <P>The majority of people on this board are great.  As I've stated elsewhere, this board is by far the best behaved and most knowledgeable forum I have encountered.<P>Most people will clean up their act, but there will continue to be those who don't.  Instead of ending an otherwise good thing, or removing what is good in this forum with too radical of changes, we need to be able to deal with those people who chronically are causing trouble effectively. <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000012||Urchin||07-04-2001||06:14 PM||||Yes, Fformula88, but how do you go about effectively discharging those who do not act appropriately?  We all know there are ways to get back on after you have been banned.  I agree with you but am wondering how you could get rid of such people on a permanent basis.  I'm just afraid that with stuff like this consistantly occuring that the end result will be that none of us will have this place to turn to for help or humor.  I don't want to see that happen<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Wannabe||07-04-2001||08:06 PM||||Very well said, and lots of valid opinions. The consensus is that this is a valuable service for all of us, and there is enough relevant discourse going on to make it worthwhile for most of the participants. It's hard to stay quited sometimes when people make ridiculous comments, but, as was suggested in another thread, maybe the best thing most of us can do is ignore the useless banter, especially when someone sees the need to target an individual.||||reg||1
